2026-09-27T07:42:47.3339347Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3339947Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3340484Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3341791Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3343348Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3343516Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3343848Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3344905Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3345425Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3345586Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3345947Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3346157Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3346466Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3347061Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3347420Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3347614Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3348031Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3348303Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3348535Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3349195Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3349813Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3350958Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3351895Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3352078Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3352816Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3353791Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3354584Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3355144Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3355888Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3356039Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3356372Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3356577Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3358792Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3361176Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3361550Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3362362Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3363614Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3365279Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3366262Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3367050Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3367790Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3367965Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3437748Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3438141Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3440069Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3442067Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3443212Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3444980Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:47.3445377Z 
